row @17,412,694,743
  col @17,483,16,600
    link "Accordion (Sections With Show/Hide Functionality)" accordion/ @17,483,16,101
    text An accordion is a vertically stacked set of interactive headings that each contain a title, content snippet, or thumbnail representing a section of content. @17,596,16,487
  col @45,523,14,520
    link Alert alert/ @45,523,14,21
    text An alert is an element that displays a brief, important message in a way that attracts the user's attention without interrupting the user's task. @45,556,14,487
  col @71,523,13,520
    link "Alert and Message Dialogs" alertdialog/ @71,523,13,82
    text An alert dialog is a modal dialog that interrupts the user's workflow to communicate an important message and acquire a response. @71,617,13,426
  col @96,564,11,438
    link Breadcrumb breadcrumb/ @96,564,11,20
    text A breadcrumb trail consists of a list of links to the parent pages of the current page in hierarchical order. @96,596,11,406
  col @119,462,17,642
    link Button button/ @119,462,17,21
    text A button is a widget that enables users to trigger an action or event, such as submitting a form, opening a dialog, canceling an action, or performing a delete operation. @119,495,17,609
  col @148,503,12,560
    link "Carousel (Slide Show or Image Rotator)" carousel/ @148,503,12,122
    text A carousel presents a set of items, referred to as slides, by sequentially displaying a subset of one or more slides. @148,637,12,426
  col @172,442,23,682
    link Checkbox checkbox/ @172,442,23,20
    text WAI-ARIA supports two types of checkbox widgets: dual-state checkboxes toggle between two choices -- checked and not checked -- and tri-state checkboxes, which allow an additional third state known as partially checked. @172,474,23,650
  col @207,655,7,256
    link Combobox combobox/ @207,655,7,21
    text A combobox is an input widget that has an associated popup. @207,688,7,223
  col @226,605,8,357
    link "Dialog (Modal)" dialog-modal/ @226,605,8,40
    text A dialog is a window overlaid on either the primary window or another dialog window. @226,657,8,305
  col @246,594,10,378
    link "Disclosure (Show/Hide)" disclosure/ @246,594,10,41
    text A disclosure is a widget that enables content to be either collapsed (hidden) or expanded (visible). @246,647,10,325
  col @268,574,10,418
    link Feed feed/ @268,574,10,20
    text A feed is a section of a page that automatically loads new sections of content as the user scrolls. @268,606,10,386
  col @290,412,19,743
    link "Grid (Interactive Tabular Data and Layout Containers)" grid/ @290,412,19,142
    text A grid widget is a container that enables users to navigate the information or interactive elements it contains using directional navigation keys, such as arrow keys, Home, and End. @290,566,19,589
  col @321,615,8,337
    link Landmarks landmarks/ @321,615,8,20
    text Landmarks are a set of eight roles that identify the major sections of a page. @321,647,8,305
  col @341,665,6,236
    link Link link/ @341,665,6,21
    text A link widget provides an interactive reference to a resource. @341,698,6,203
  col @359,574,9,418
    link Listbox listbox/ @359,574,9,20
    text A listbox widget presents a list of options and allows a user to select one or more of them. @359,606,9,386
  col @380,523,10,520
    link "Menu and Menubar" menubar/ @380,523,10,61
    text A menu is a widget that offers a list of choices to the user, such as a set of actions or functions. @380,596,10,447
  col @402,574,9,418
    link "Menu Button" menu-button/ @402,574,9,41
    text A menu button is a button that opens a menu as described in the Menu and Menubar Pattern. @402,627,9,365
  col @423,605,9,357
    link Meter meter/ @423,605,9,20
    text A meter is a graphical display of a numeric value that varies within a defined range. @423,637,9,325
  col @444,483,14,600
    link "Radio Group" radio/ @444,483,14,40
    text A radio group is a set of checkable buttons, known as radio buttons, where no more than one of the buttons can be checked at a time. @444,535,14,548
  col @470,605,8,357
    link Slider slider/ @470,605,8,20
    text A slider is an input where the user selects a value from within a given range. @470,637,8,325
  col @490,574,11,418
    link "Slider (Multi-Thumb)" slider-multithumb/ @490,574,11,41
    text A multi-thumb slider implements the Slider Pattern but includes two or more thumbs, often on a single rail. @490,627,11,365
  col @513,584,9,398
    link Spinbutton spinbutton/ @513,584,9,21
    text A spinbutton is an input widget that restricts its value to a set or range of discrete values. @513,617,9,365
  col @534,584,8,398
    link Switch switch/ @534,584,8,21
    text A switch is an input widget that allows users to choose one of two values: on or off. @534,617,8,365
  col @554,452,18,662
    link Table table/ @554,452,18,21
    text Like an HTML table element, a WAI-ARIA table is a static tabular structure containing one or more rows that each contain one or more cells; it is not an interactive widget. @554,485,18,629
  col @584,544,11,479
    link Tabs tabs/ @584,544,11,20
    text Tabs are a set of layered sections of content, known as tab panels, that display one panel of content at a time. @584,576,11,447
  col @607,594,10,378
    link Toolbar toolbar/ @607,594,10,21
    text A toolbar is a container for grouping a set of controls, such as buttons, menubuttons, or checkboxes. @607,627,10,345
  col @629,523,15,520
    link Tooltip tooltip/ @629,523,15,21
    text A tooltip is a popup that displays information related to an element when the element receives keyboard focus or the mouse hovers over it. @629,556,15,487
  col @656,676,4,215
    link "Tree View" treeview/ @656,676,4,40
    text A tree view widget presents a hierarchical list. @656,728,4,163
  col @672,594,12,378
    link Treegrid treegrid/ @672,594,12,21
    text A treegrid widget presents a hierarchical data grid consisting of tabular information that is editable or interactive. @672,627,12,345
  col @696,493,15,580
    link "Window Splitter" windowsplitter/ @696,493,15,41
    text A window splitter is a moveable separator between two sections, or panes, of a window that enables users to change the relative size of the panes. @696,546,15,527
